Assumption challenged:
  The table entries should not be promoted to a group law on isomorphism classes.
  The useful object is a quotient map with a visible missing-coordinate fiber.
  In LRC14 terms, c is a canary/filler coordinate: legal if fixed and audited, illegal if erased.
